\textbf{DOK 3 TASK QUESTIONS}

\vspace{1em}

\noindent \textbullet \ \textbf{Entry / Access (build understanding, low floor)}
\begin{itemize}[label=$\bullet$, leftmargin=0.5in]
    \item What do you notice about how each school's enrollment is changing over time?
    \item How are the situations for School A and School B similar? How are they different?
    \item What does a 2\% decrease look like over time? What about a 3\% increase?
    \item If you had to describe each school's trend in words, what would you say?
\end{itemize}

\vspace{1em}

\noindent \textbullet \ \textbf{Developing (connect representations, reasoning)}
\begin{itemize}[label=$\bullet$, leftmargin=0.5in]
    \item How could you represent each school's enrollment with a function or model? Explain your thinking.
    \item What patterns do you expect to see if you track enrollment over several years? Why?
    \item How does the starting value affect the future of each school's enrollment?
    \item What role does the rate (2\% vs 3\%) play in how the enrollments change?
\end{itemize}

\vspace{1em}

\noindent \textbullet \ \textbf{Core Task (DOK 3 -- reasoning \& justification)}
\begin{itemize}[label=$\bullet$, leftmargin=0.5in]
    \item Will School B eventually overtake School A? Justify your answer using mathematical reasoning.
    \item About when do you think the enrollments will be equal? How could you estimate or determine that?
    \item How do the structure and behavior of exponential growth vs. decay help you make predictions here?
    \item What assumptions are you making when you compare these two situations?
\end{itemize}

\vspace{1em}

\noindent \textbullet \ \textbf{Extension (higher-level thinking, generalization)}
\begin{itemize}[label=$\bullet$, leftmargin=0.5in]
    \item How would your conclusion change if the rates were different? What thresholds matter?
    \item Can you create a general rule for when a decreasing quantity will be overtaken by an increasing one?
    \item How sensitive is the outcome to small changes in the percentages or starting values? Explain.
    \item What real-world factors might make this model less accurate over time?
\end{itemize}

\vspace{1em}

\noindent \textbullet \ \textbf{Discussion / Argumentation prompts (to support collaboration)}
\begin{itemize}[label=$\bullet$, leftmargin=0.5in]
    \item Do you agree or disagree with your partner's prediction? Why?
    \item What evidence best supports your conclusion?
    \item Can there be more than one reasonable approach to solving this? Compare them.
\end{itemize}

