% ROW 1: Do Now
\textbf{Do Now (5 minutes)} \newline\newline Vocabulary builder -- 5 minutes & 
Project DoNow/Announcement slide that has the vocabulary activity (matching) \newline\newline
\scriptsize
Discuss growth and decay in a general sense. Discuss how the terms growth and decay could apply to the graphs of $y = 2^x$ and $y = 0.5^x$. Have students match the following terms and definitions.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*., leftmargin=*, nosep]
    \item An equation modeled by a function of the form $y = ab^x$ with $0 < b < 1$. \textbf{[exponential decay]}
    \item An equation modeled by a function of the form $y = ab^x$ with $b > 1$. \textbf{[exponential growth]}
    \item The base of an exponential growth function. \textbf{[growth factor]}
    \item The base of an exponential decay function. \textbf{[decay factor]}
\end{enumerate} \normalsize & 
Read the slide and obtain materials for the class. \newline\newline
Complete vocabulary activity. & 
How can you engage students in the lesson? \newline\newline
How can you hook them? \newline\newline
How are all adults intentionally planned for? \\
\hline

% ROW 2: Launch
\textbf{Launch (10 minutes):}
\begin{itemize}[label=$\bullet$, leftmargin=*, nosep]
    \item Unpacking objectives
    \item Entry point to new content
    \item Check for understanding
    \item Teach/Review skill necessary for Explore
    \item Academic Conversation
    \item Clear role for all adults
\end{itemize} & 
Read the Explore \& Reason aloud and instruct students to think about the question from A) describe how the value of the car decreases from year to year. \textbf{(Start TWPS - 2} minutes independent think/write, 2 minutes share with their partner\textbf{)} \newline\newline
Circulate to watch what individual students are recording then circulate to listen to pair conversations to identify a few students to share out their thinking (elicit the idea of the value of the car decreasing NON-linearly $\rightarrow$ exponentially) \newline\newline
Tiered questions to consider asking students:
\begin{itemize}[label=$\bullet$, leftmargin=*, nosep]
    \item What do you notice about the value of the car?
    \item How could you determine the relationship between the consecutive values of the car?
    \item For struggling learners: How is knowing the general form of the exponential function helpful in describing this situation?
    \item For early finishers (extension): Write the function that models the value of the car after $x$ years. How long will it take for the car to be worth $1/4$ of its original value? How long will it take if the car depreciates twice as fast?
    \item What is something else that depreciates?
\end{itemize} \vspace{1em}
Read content/language objectives aloud (connecting to what was previously learned) & 
Actively listen to the read aloud and record ideas of how the value of the car is changing each year and then pairing up with designated partner to share ideas. \newline\newline\newline\newline\newline\newline\newline
\textbf{TWPS} \newline
Record thoughts/do calculations to explore the value of the car over time (independently) \newline\newline\newline\newline\newline
Pair up and share their thinking with a partner (use of sentence starters for ELs as needed) \newline\newline
Actively listen & 
What will you explicitly model and how? \newline\newline
How will you know if students are ready to work alone? \newline\newline
How are all adults intentionally planned for? \\
\hline

